  "difference": "The same workload put 9 transactions on the base layer through the public rail (0.30 per call) and 0 through Wakeless (0.00 per call); from the public rail's transactions alone an observer rebuilt 3 of 3 vendors, 100.00% of the spend and the order of first contact, because the open names the payer and the payTo, the claim carries the voucher's cumulative amount in clear, and the payout names the recipient. For Wakeless the base layer shows vault deposits and withdrawals only, and the run itself added none: every deposit and every redemption the enclave accepted was a private transfer inside MagicBlock's Private Ephemeral Rollup, and a redemption it refused moved nothing, so the ledger holds nothing from the run, and no vault deposit or withdrawal by any party landed in the window. What remains recoverable is the edge of the pool, not the relationship: a vault deposit, when the buyer makes one, names the buyer and an amount going in, and a vault withdrawal names a vendor and an amount coming out, but nothing on the ledger joins the two, so the observer rebuilt 0 of 3 vendors and 0.00% of the spend; with one buyer and few vendors in the pool, timing and amounts at those edges are the residual risk. The privacy claim is against the public ledger, not against the operators: the facilitator sees the vouchers and the channels, MagicBlock's enclave sees the private transfers, and NEAR's private shard sees a funding's origin and route when a channel is funded through Aurora; each of the three sees inside, and none of what they see reaches the ledger.",
